to employ single crystal $\mathrm{\DeltaX}$ -ray crystallography to pinpoint these installed functional groups. The excellent stability also ensures that the obtained MTV-MOFs will be stable and usable under relatively harsh conditions. Overall, the inherent ‘pockets’, flexibility, and high stability make PCN-700 an optimal platform for implementing the SLI strategy.
To carry out SLI, PCN-700 crystals were sequentially exposed to a solution of $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BDC}$ and $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{M}\mathrm{e}_{2}$ -TPDC in DMF at 75 $\mathrm{{}^{\circ}C}$ for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ . The afforded crystals were washed with fresh DMF before $\mathrm{\DeltaX}$ -ray single crystal diffraction data collection. The existence and position of BDC and $\mathbf{Me}_{2}$ -TPDC are unambiguously observed in the crystallographically resolved structure. The resultant structure, designated as PCN-703 (Figure 3d), crystallizes in the $P4_{2}/m n m$ space group. Interestingly, the unit cell of PCN-703 is doubled in size compared to the prototype MOF (PCN-700) due to the asymmetric distribution of $\mathbf{Me}_{2}$ -TPDC linker which eliminates a mirror plane passing though the $\mathbf{Zr}_{6}$ cluster. In PCN-703, each $\mathrm{Zr}_{6}$ cluster is 11-connected to eight $\mathbf{Me}_{2}$ -BPDC, two BDC, and one $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{e}_{2}$ -TPDC linkers. The overall composition can be formulated as $\mathrm{Zr_{6}O_{4}(O H)_{5}(H_{2}O)(M e_{2}\mathrm{-}B P D C)_{8}B D C_{2}(M e_{2}\mathrm{-}T P D C)}$ , which has been further confirmed by $\mathrm{^{1}H}$ -NMR. The bulk material maintains its crystallinity and porosity after SLI, which is supported by well-retained powder $\mathrm{x}$ -ray diffraction patterns (Figure S6) and ${\bf N}_{2}$ gas adsorption-desorption isotherms (Figure S13).
It should be noted that the sequence of the installation is crucial for the success of SLI. As shown in Figure 3, starting with a short linker, the BDC will occupy all the small pockets (pocket B) with an $\scriptstyle0\cdots0$ distance of $\mathbf{\hat{7.0\A}}$ , leaving the large pockets (pocket A') unoccupied. Pocket A' has an $\scriptstyle0\cdots0$ distance of $\bar{16.5\mathrm{~\AA~}}$ , which is slightly longer than the size of $\mathbf{Me}_{2}.$ - TPDC (15.2 Å). Further incorporated ${\bf M e}_{2}–\mathrm{TPDC}$ will only occupy every other pocket $\mathbf{A^{\prime}}$ and stretch the other pocket $\mathbf{A^{\prime}}$ to $17.{\dot{4}}{\dot{\mathrm{A}}}$ (pocket A''). As a result, a MOF with three linkers of different lengths is obtained. However, if the $\mathbf{Me}_{2}$ -TPDC linkers are installed first, they will occupy all the pockets A and meanwhile stretch the pocket B to $\overset{\cdot}{8.2\mathrm{~\AA~}}$ (pocket B'). Therefore, it is impossible to install BDC into these elongated pockets (pocket B') because the length of BDC is only $7.0\mathring\mathrm{A}$ .
With the successful stepwise synthesis of PCN-703, we believe functionalized linkers should also be usable for this strategy and the resulting MTV-MOFs should possess the same topology as long as the lengths of linkers are not altered. As a proof of concept, two functionalized linkers, $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ - BDC (2-amino-1,4-benzenedicarboxylate) and $\mathrm{(CH_{3}O)_{2}}$ - TPDC $(2^{\prime},5^{\prime}$ -dimethoxyterphenyl- $\cdot4,4"$ -dicarboxylate), were installed using the SLI strategy, which gave rise  to a new MTV-MOF, namely PCN-704. It exhibits identical topology to PCN-703. Single crystal $\mathrm{\DeltaX}$ -ray crystallography and $\mathrm{^1H}$ - NMR clearly indicate the existence and proper ratio of $\mathrm{NH}_{2}.$ - BDC and $\left(\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{O}\right)_{2}$ -TPDC. By using the SLI strategy, we successfully demonstrated an ordered MTV-MOF fabrication with amino groups, methoxyl groups, and methyl groups precisely arranged.
In summary, we have developed a unique strategy, Sequential Linker Installation (SLI), to construct multivariate MOFs with functional groups precisely located. Single crystal to single crystal transformation is realized and the positions of the subsequently installed linkers are pinpointed. SLI is a powerful methodology to introduce multiple functional groups into MOFs in a controlled and crystallographically ordered manner, particularly for those based on hard Lewis acidic metal species. In light of their structural adaptability and high chemical stability, we anticipate SLI will have a variety of applications, especially when specific functional groups in proper proximity are desired.
